Z||000032||Slammed Fiero||08-02-2001||03:49 PM||||Wheels came from Tire Rack , they were $215 a piece. The tires are Pirelli P Zero C's (C for competition).<P>as for the coilover question earlier , I have a set of modified ground control coilovers in rear on Koni struts I modified the coilovers for my autocross/track use , 325lbs rating which is really stiff for a street car. Ie with the Koni's set on soft a 180lbs person can't move the car down .5 of an inch.. Very stiff. For street I would go with 275lbs. The front has Carrera custom rate springs.<P>My setup is neutral , keep in mind huge 255/40's out back help keep it that way. You have to get the back of a 84 to 87 Fiero as stiff as you can for the car to really handle and dial out understeer. Stock fiero's have a lot of hobby horsing of the chassis and lots of understeer/ trailing throttle oversteer..all bad words when it comes to cornering. A rear sway bar makes a difference on a Fiero, but not as much as people would like to think.<P>JM ||||reg||1
